<td id="A3.T8.4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.0539(+16.66%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.1980(+10.43%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.3143(+6.72%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.7123(+3.82%)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CCT</span></th>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.0248(+13.76%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.0729(+10.79%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.1050(+6.59%)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.4.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T8.4.1.3.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.2706(+4.08%)</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess cross-dataset adaptability, we pre-train PANTHER on WeChatPay and fine-tune it on MBD-mini and CCT. Table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ C.2 Data-Level Transferability ‣ Appendix C Transferability of PANTHER ‣ PANTHER: Generative Pretraining Beyond Language for Sequential User Behavior Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows an average HR@1 improvement of 16.66%, demonstrating effective transfer of our generative pretraining across diverse transaction contexts. The model retains valuable cross-data signals, such as user spending patterns, even when the merchant or product space changes.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Ablation Experiments</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To examine the sensitivity of PANTHER to the balance between <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{CL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{CL}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we vary the loss coefficient <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and report the corresponding performance. The results are summarized in <a href="#A4.T9" title="In Appendix D Ablation Experiments ‣ PANTHER: Generative Pretraining Beyond Language for Sequential User Behavior Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Performance on WeChat Pay under different values of the loss coefficient <math id="A4.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
